Doom host test: runs the real doom.pico code (Doom sources + pico layer,
unmodified) on 64-bit Linux against a syscall-only fake kernel.

  ./build.sh                  build it (needs the WAD at ../../doom1.wad)
  ./doomtest -timedemo demo1  replay demo1..3, prints gametics + fps
  ./doomtest                  attract loop (Ctrl-C to stop)
  asm32/runtest.sh            validate the 386 fixed-point assembly

out/frame_NNNN.ppm holds every 50th frame; out/ collects files Doom
writes (default.cfg on a clean quit). See docs/DOOM.md.
